# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Lighthouse / browser-tooling output.
# `.lighthouseci/` holds the raw LHR JSON+HTML that `npx lhci autorun` writes
# (16 pages, ~8 MB), and `.cache/` holds the Puppeteer browser download.
# Both are regenerable from `npx lhci autorun --config=tools/lighthouserc.js`;
# the scores that matter are recorded in
# docs/reviews/reproducibility-and-performance-report.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.lighthouseci/
.cache/
docs/reviews/lighthouse/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Measurement-harness output.
# tools/ holds the scripts and IS committed (see tools/README.md). artifacts/
# holds what they write — capture distributions, hover audits, CLS probes,
# style/layout traces, subset fonts and the logs from `make reproduce`. All of
# it is regenerable, so committing it would bloat the repo and go stale.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
artifacts/
tools/evidence/retired-tools/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ephemeral editor test artifacts.
# `.ff_screenshots/` lives at the repo root and holds throwaway diagnostic
# scripts (take_screenshots.js, test_ff.js, verify_editor.js) plus their
# generated outputs (PNGs, ff_results.json, editor_context_panel_results.json,
# cascade_check_results.json). These are scratch outputs for the local
# browser-based layout/audit checks, are large (~6 MB of PNGs) and host-specific,
# so they are kept out of git rather than committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.ff_screenshots/

